  "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/medicine_committee_terra_round2_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B045",
        "laureates": [
          "Douglas R. Lowy",
          "Ian H. Frazer",
          "John T. Schiller"
        ],
        "citation": "for virus-like-particle vaccines that prevent HPV infection and related cancers"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B022",
    "B024"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "My configuration is unchanged. B045 most strongly combines a delimited vaccine-enabling principle with mature, durable prevention of HPV infection and related cancers. Its medical consequence is direct and established, and Lowy, Frazer, and Schiller remain a plausible three-person configuration for the VLP-centered achievement, provided the citation remains confined to that work rather than encompassing the whole pathway of papillomavirus research, product development, and implementation.",
    "case_against": "The attribution issue remains material. The supplied evidence does not resolve the respective indispensable contributions to papillomavirus biology, VLP research, vaccine design, clinical development, and implementation. The proposed allocation therefore requires a detailed historical priority review before it could be regarded as final.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "linnarsson-sten",
        "point": "Linnarsson retains GLP-1 physiology and incretin therapies as the leading configuration because of their fundamental endocrine basis and transformative, mature effects in diabetes and obesity, while recognizing difficult attribution boundaries.",
        "response": "I agree that B022 has exceptional clinical importance and an unusually persuasive physiology-to-therapy trajectory. I retain B045 narrowly because prevention of infection and related cancers is a long-established outcome of a more specifically framed vaccine-enabling principle. B022's boundary among hormone identification, physiological interpretation, therapeutic engineering, and pharmaceutical development remains comparably consequential and unresolved."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "sandberg-rickard",
        "point": "Sandberg argues that B024 merits priority as a deeply validated, fundamental mechanism of ER-stress sensing and adaptation with a compact proposed attribution to Mori and Walter.",
        "response": "B024 remains the strongest basic-science alternative: its mechanistic clarity, maturity, and focused attribution are substantial advantages. I agree that its case should rest on the discovery itself rather than broad asserted disease relevance. In this comparison, however, I give greater weight to B045's demonstrated preventive medical outcome, while retaining the need for equally rigorous scrutiny of its proposed credit."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "wahren-herlenius-marie",
        "point": "Wahren-Herlenius favors TNF blockade because Feldmann and Maini connect a pathogenic mechanism to a durable, disease-modifying treatment principle, while cautioning against conflating their contribution with wider anti-TNF development.",
        "response": "The focused mechanism-to-treatment character of B013 is compelling, and the stated caution on attribution is well taken. B045 nevertheless has the stronger overall combination of a discrete biological-technical advance and enduring population-level prevention, subject to the same requirement that the public record distinguish the VLP discovery from subsequent development and delivery."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether detailed historical assessment supports Lowy, Frazer, and Schiller as the essential recipients for the specifically VLP-centered discovery after separating adjacent contributions.",
      "Whether B022 can define an equally discrete awardable achievement and recipient allocation without crediting later pharmaceutical development.",
      "How the committee should ultimately balance B024's fundamental and compact mechanism against B045's directly demonstrated preventive benefit."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "No candidate-specific conflict is apparent from the supplied profile. My documented collaborations and institutional affiliations identify no connection to the proposed recipients."
  }
}
